summary:
Iteration 21 — Auth (JWT+RBAC) + Audit stamping + Assistant honorifics/screen-context/navigation. Created /app/backend/tests/test_iter21_auth_audit_assistant.py with 25 tests across 8 classes covering every item in the review request. Result: 25/25 pass (100%). All 3 seed users authenticate correctly, RBAC works (Staff/Carrier get 403 on /auth/users and /auth/register), Admin-only PATCH/DELETE gated, admin-cannot-delete-self returns 400, change-password 401 on wrong current + full roundtrip works. Bullion writes stamp created_by=kishan/modified_by=kishan/entry_source=manual by default and 'ai' via X-Entry-Source header; PUT correctly preserves created_by while updating modified_by (verified staff editing a kishan-created trip). Bullion transactions auto-generate TXN-### and carry audit fields. Proxy audit injection: POST /api/parties (remote) succeeds as kishan (role fixed to 'customer' — remote schema didn't accept 'buyer'). Assistant chat honors both Sir and Boss honorifics, echoes screen_context (referenced 'INV-042' and 'Lalit'), and emits a JSON action=navigate block with route=/invoices for nav intent. /api/wingman/health still returns ok. IMPORTANT bug discovered while parsing SSE: /api/assistant/chat emits multi-line Claude content via `yield f"data: {content}

"` — when content itself contains `

` (e.g. around ```json ... ``` blocks) the SSE frame terminator gets injected mid-frame, so standard SSE parsers on the client see the JSON tool-call as an orphan message body outside any data frame. The frontend tool-call parser will therefore fail to extract navigate/add_bag/etc. blocks reliably.

critical.issue:
SSE-framing bug: server yields `data: {event.content}

` but Claude's text chunks can contain embedded `

` (e.g. around fenced ```json``` tool blocks). The embedded blank line terminates the SSE frame prematurely, so subsequent content leaks outside any `data:` frame. Standard SSE parsers (EventSource in the browser, Expo's fetch-based reader) will drop the JSON tool-call block entirely. Fix: escape newlines in event.content (replace 
 with a placeholder or emit one `data:` line per newline-split segment) OR base64-encode chunks. Reference: /app/backend/server.py:851 `yield f"data: {event.content}

"`

rca_of_issue:
SSE-framing bug on /api/assistant/chat: root cause is line `yield f"data: {event.content}

"` in server.py::assistant_chat.event_gen. Claude Sonnet's TextDelta.content can contain arbitrary characters including `

`. Per SSE spec (https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#server-sent-events), an empty line terminates the current message. Injecting the model's newlines directly into the wire format therefore produces malformed multi-message frames. Reproduction: POST /api/assistant/chat with `{"session_id":"x","message":"मुझे invoices पर ले चलो","honorific":"Sir"}` and observe the raw stream — the ```json ... ``` block sits between two blank lines, outside any `data:` prefix. Mitigation options: (a) split content on '
' and emit one `data:` line per segment then a single blank terminator; (b) JSON-encode the content: `yield f'data: {json.dumps({"t":event.content})}

'` (client decodes); (c) base64 the payload.
